title: Bridge scraped Langertha::Runtime::Metrics into Langfuse OTLP metrics
updated: 2026-08-13T03:43:02Z
---

karr #29 ships the scraping side (Langertha::Role::Runtime::MetricsPoll -> Langertha::Runtime::Metrics) but stops short of exporting the parsed records anywhere. Langfuse has a metrics-generation API that was fairly new at the time of the original ticket and was deliberately deferred to avoid guessing the wire shape.

What needs doing:
- Confirm the current Langfuse metrics API surface (HTTP OTLP endpoint or REST) and the payload shape (resourceMetrics / scopeMetrics / metric{ name, type, value, labels }).
- Add a `bridge_to_langfuse` (or similar) method on Langertha::Role::Runtime::MetricsPoll that takes parsed records + a trace context and submits them, OR an OTLP exporter that the caller can wire up.
- Decide whether to ship via Langfuse's /api/public/metrics endpoint or generic OTLP HTTP (Langfuse accepts the latter for self-hosted setups).
- Extend the existing live test to assert against a self-hosted Langfuse if one is up.

Out of scope here:
- Remote-write adapter to a Prometheus server (separate ticket; the scraping side is generic).
- Langfuse metrics for non-Prometheus engines (Ollama /api/ps adapter, also separate).

Refs: karr #29
